    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Ideally located on Emmet Street, this substantial mid-terrace period residence extends to approximately 150 m² and offers generous accommodation, extensive external space and a range of valuable outbuildings in a highly convenient central location. The accommodation extends over three floors and comprises a kitchen with dining area, sitting room, living room, six bedrooms, bathroom, and separate wc. \n\nThe property is well maintained and immediately habitable, while offering considerable scope for a new owner to modernise. The property retains its period character, with PVC sash windows to the front elevation. A particular feature of the property is the extensive external space, including a large rear yard with double-gated vehicular access, extensive gardens, and a range of outbuildings including a barn, forge, and fuel shed. \n\nThe combination of the yard, gardens, vehicular access and outbuildings provides a generous range of additional external space and offers considerable flexibility for parking, storage, workshop use and other purposes. The substantial rear garden extends approximately 8 metres in width and 28 metres in length, extending to the rear boundary wall.\n\nThe property has benefited from a number of significant upgrades, including insulation works and a complete electrical rewire throughout. \n\nHaving been vacant for over three years, the property may potentially qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to Terms and Conditions of the Grant. Conveniently located within walking distance of the town centre, train station, schools, shops, healthcare facilities, and sporting amenities, this property offers an attractive combination of substantial accommodation, period character, extensive gardens, outbuildings and direct vehicular access in a central location.\n\nThe property would appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, owner-occupiers and investors. With six bedrooms and approximately 150 m² of accommodation, this is a particularly versatile property offering the opportunity to acquire a well-maintained period home that is ready to occupy, while also providing scope for modernisation over time. \n\nFull details and viewings on request.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (5.25ft x 27.89ft) With carpet flooring <br>Dining Room (12.80ft x 11.15ft) With open fireplace and carpet flooring.<br>Kitchen (13.78ft x 11.15ft) With lino covered flooring and solid fuel range<br>Downstairs WC (3.18ft x 6.89ft) Tiled with wc and wash hand basin.<br>Living Room (12.14ft x 13.12ft) With solid fuel stove and carpet flooring.<br>Landing (4.92ft x 20.34ft) With carpet flooring and access to all first floor rooms. <br>Bathroom (4.92ft x 9.51ft) Tiled bathroom with wc, vanity unit, and electric shower over bath.<br>Master Bedroom (10.17ft x 12.80ft) With carpet flooring and feature fireplace.<br>Bedroom 2 (10.50ft x 7.87ft) With carpet flooring.<br>Bedroom 3 (8.86ft x 8.53ft) With carpet flooring and vanity unit.<br>Bedroom 4 (9.84ft x 7.55ft) With carpet flooring and vanity unit.<br>Bedroom 5 (10.17ft x 5.25ft) With carpet flooring and vanity unit<br>Bedroom 6 (9.51ft x 16.40ft) With carpet flooring.<br>Other (8.14ft x 24.25ft) Gateway<br>Outbuildings (24.93ft x 15.42ft) Large storage shed.<br>Outbuildings (16.40ft x 11.81ft) Middle shed<br>Outbuildings (11.81ft x 12.14ft) Old forge "
      },
